   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Working with Data: Data Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-08-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which one of these is part of the data preparation process?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Model validation</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Data preparation is about cleaning and transforming data so it is ready for analysis and modeling.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Classification</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Preparing data means cleaning and transforming it before analysis and modeling.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Cleaning</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Cleaning is a key part of getting data ready for analysis and modeling.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-08-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Why is data preparation so important?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>It makes models more accurate</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Data that has been cleaned improves the accuracy of models that rely on it.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>It's not important</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Dirty data causes problems in analysis and modeling, so cleaning it matters.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Computers can help clean the data</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Code can help with cleaning, but that is not why it matters. Clean data makes models more accurate.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-08-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is a goal of data cleaning?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Fixing formatting issues</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Fixing formatting is a goal, but so is fixing data types. Both are cleaning goals.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Fixing data types</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Fixing data types is a goal, but so is fixing other formatting, like whitespace and dates.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>All of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Cleaning fixes formatting problems, such as whitespace, dates and data types.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-08-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Merging or joining two datasets into one can affect consistency in data</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Datasets from different sources need a common standard so the merged data stays useful.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. When datasets from different sources are merged, each needs a common standard to keep the data consistent.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-08-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What's the first thing that should be done when faced with missing data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Delete it</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Deleting is one option, but the right fix depends on why the data went missing.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Assess why it's missing</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. How you fix missing data depends on how and why it went missing.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Try to fill in empty values</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Filling in values is one option, but first find out why the data is missing.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-08-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Joining two or more datasets can cause which following issue(s)?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Duplicates</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Duplicates are one issue, but data from different sources can also be formatted differently.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Inconsistent formatting</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Formatting is one issue, but joining datasets also commonly creates duplicates.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>All of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Joining can create duplicates, and data from different sources can be formatted differently.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
